00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:13.580
group you are talking and also what sort of
underlying implications you think it points

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.120
to about the economy at large.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:16.120
Speaker 3: Yeah, exactly.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:20.370
I mean, you know, economists will will say,
oh, well, house prices going up is good because

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:24.290
you're going to have the wealth effect of
people feeling wealthier because their house

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.290
is worth more.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:29.610
So be, you know, taking equity out of that
house and going on spending it in the economy,

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:30.790
which is good for the economy.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.380
I mean, fine.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:36.130
Obviously, if you would see a massive fall
